01:11:03,157 --> 01:11:09,157
Lone Star is a 1996 American neo-Western mystery film
written, edited, and directed by John Sayles.

11
01:18:09,473 --> 01:18:15,473
Set in a small town in South Texas, the film deals with a sheriff's (played by Chris Cooper)
investigation into the murder of one of his predecessors (Kris Kristofferson) decades earlier.

12
01:25:15,789 --> 01:25:21,789
The cast also stars Joe Morton, Elizabeth Peña, Clifton James, Ron
Canada, Frances McDormand and Matthew McConaughey.

13
01:32:22,105 --> 01:32:28,105
The film premiered at the 1996 South by Southwest Festival and received widespread critical acclaim, with critics
regarding it as a high point of 1990s independent cinema as well as one of Sayles's best films.

14
01:39:28,421 --> 01:39:34,421
Sayles's screenplay was nominated for an Academy Award,
BAFTA Award, and Golden Globe Award.

15
01:46:34,736 --> 01:46:40,736
The film was also nominated for four Independent Spirit Awards,
with Elizabeth Peña winning Best Supporting Female.

16
01:53:41,052 --> 01:53:47,052
Lone Star was recognized by the American Film Institute in AFI's 10
Top 10 list in 2008 as a nominated Western Film.

17
02:00:47,368 --> 02:00:53,368
The film explores themes of sheriff, texas, family
secrets, neo-western, dark secret.

18
02:07:53,684 --> 02:07:59,684
The tone is mind_bending and dark and emotional.
